From 86e9ef5927ef0805cb6ff898b1673bc7511b2cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jky72 <jky72@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:08:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] chore: checkpoint the IME, render-pipeline and
 shader-init work

Working-tree checkpoint of everything in flight, not a reviewed change set.

Input method
- Stamp the composition (preedit) into the cell buffer and let the normal cell
  renderer draw it, so font, size, DPI and wide-cell spacing come out right by
  construction. Adds src/app/render_pipeline/ime_stamp.rs and
  src/app/window_manager/ime_composition.rs (Imm32 observer with HWND subclass
  chaining), retires the egui overlay path for preedit.

Custom background shader
- Build the render pipeline on a worker thread. The driver compile of a large
  shader takes seconds and needs no window, so the window now paints its first
  frame immediately and the shader blends in when it is ready. Measured on this
  machine: first frame 8.4s -> 1.6s.
- Isolate the installer's GLSL-frontend limitation that broke such shaders:
  naga does not resolve GLSL prototypes, so every function must be defined
  before its first call.

Also includes render-pipeline plumbing, config and settings-UI changes, and
vendor/par-term-emu-core-rust terminal changes that were pending in the tree.
